1
00:01:35,220 --> 00:01:38,640
Oh, fuck. Fuck!

2
00:01:45,855 --> 00:01:47,148
Are you sure it's him?

3
00:01:47,148 --> 00:01:49,067
<i>I saw him hit the pavement.</i>

4
00:01:49,067 --> 00:01:51,778
Maruyama-san,
before Nakahara fell,

5
00:01:51,778 --> 00:01:54,072
I saw Tozawa enter
the building.

6
00:01:54,072 --> 00:01:56,032
Do you have photos of that?

7
00:01:56,032 --> 00:01:58,118
No. But he was there.

8
00:02:00,662 --> 00:02:03,748
Fine.
We'll include that detail.

9
00:02:03,748 --> 00:02:05,333
Start dictating.

10
00:02:13,383 --> 00:02:15,135
Answer me.

11
00:02:15,135 --> 00:02:17,429
What were you looking for
in my study?

12
00:02:17,429 --> 00:02:18,930
Nothing.

13
00:02:18,930 --> 00:02:21,725
I was curious to see
where you live, where you work.

14
00:02:23,977 --> 00:02:25,645
Don't lie to me.

15
00:02:25,645 --> 00:02:27,022
I'm not lying to you.

16
00:02:27,022 --> 00:02:28,023
I'm not a stupid man.

17
00:02:28,023 --> 00:02:30,233
I'm not--
come on, I was just--

18
00:02:30,233 --> 00:02:31,735
oh, okay.

19
00:02:31,735 --> 00:02:34,195
What the fuck?

20
00:02:40,577 --> 00:02:42,579
What's on this?

21
00:02:42,579 --> 00:02:45,206
Did you photograph
my blueprints?

22
00:02:48,251 --> 00:02:50,962
I don't understand.

23
00:02:50,962 --> 00:02:53,089
What use is my work to you?

24
00:02:56,009 --> 00:02:59,429
My club is half-owned
by the Yakuza.

25
00:02:59,429 --> 00:03:01,473
They found out
about your project.

26
00:03:01,473 --> 00:03:03,183
They asked me
to get the information.

27
00:03:03,183 --> 00:03:07,604
I said I would if they give me
the club, free and clear.

28
00:03:07,604 --> 00:03:09,898
So you did it for yourself.

29
00:03:09,898 --> 00:03:11,274
Yes.

30
00:03:11,274 --> 00:03:14,527
And for the girls, too,
to protect them.

31
00:03:14,527 --> 00:03:16,446
I see.

32
00:03:16,446 --> 00:03:18,031
For the girls.

33
00:03:18,031 --> 00:03:21,034
And my career gets ruined
in the process.

34
00:03:22,660 --> 00:03:24,329
You can sleep on the couch.

35
00:03:24,329 --> 00:03:26,956
It's too late
to drive you home.

36
00:03:26,956 --> 00:03:28,833
We'll discuss this tomorrow.

37
00:06:16,918 --> 00:06:19,921
<i>Oi! Oi! Oi!</i>

38
00:07:20,148 --> 00:07:21,608
Come with me.

39
00:07:43,797 --> 00:07:48,301
Masa-san, I am so sorry.

40
00:07:48,301 --> 00:07:50,804
I won't tell them what I saw.

41
00:07:50,804 --> 00:07:54,099
I'll say you caught me first,
that I couldn't find anything.

42
00:07:54,099 --> 00:07:56,768
Ishida will have
to accept that.

43
00:07:56,768 --> 00:07:58,478
And what if
you do not provide Ishida

44
00:07:58,478 --> 00:08:01,064
with the location?

45
00:08:01,064 --> 00:08:02,399
What will he do to you?

46
00:08:02,399 --> 00:08:04,275
That's not your problem.

47
00:08:04,275 --> 00:08:05,985
I got myself into this mess.

48
00:08:05,985 --> 00:08:07,654
I'll get myself out.

49
00:08:11,408 --> 00:08:14,452
There's another project
I'm working on,

50
00:08:14,452 --> 00:08:17,163
early stages.

51
00:08:17,163 --> 00:08:21,584
If Ishida bought surrounding
properties there instead,

52
00:08:21,584 --> 00:08:23,962
he could make
a significant return.

53
00:08:25,171 --> 00:08:26,798
But you'd still be ruined.

54
00:08:26,798 --> 00:08:28,091
Maybe not.

55
00:08:28,091 --> 00:08:32,220
Unlike Shimbashi,
this one is a private venture.

56
00:08:32,220 --> 00:08:34,639
If there was a run
on nearby real estate,

57
00:08:34,639 --> 00:08:38,852
the owners would profit
and likely ask no questions.

58
00:08:40,270 --> 00:08:42,480
If we convinced Ishida
to accept this,

59
00:08:42,480 --> 00:08:47,068
you could keep your club,
and I could keep my job.

60
00:08:50,280 --> 00:08:52,407
What if I could get
someone I know

61
00:08:52,407 --> 00:08:57,120
to publish the location
of your project in the press?

62
00:08:57,120 --> 00:08:58,288
Wouldn't that make

63
00:08:58,288 --> 00:09:01,750
the Shimbashi information
worthless?

64
00:09:01,750 --> 00:09:05,170
And then I could make
my proposal

65
00:09:05,170 --> 00:09:08,548
of a valuable replacement.

66
00:09:08,548 --> 00:09:10,258
Why are you helping me?

67
00:09:14,262 --> 00:09:17,015
I know what it is
to need forgiveness.

68
00:09:24,522 --> 00:09:26,024
Thank you
for the call last night.

69
00:09:26,024 --> 00:09:28,860
It was smart of you
not to talk to anyone else.

70
00:09:28,860 --> 00:09:31,279
Of course.

71
00:09:31,279 --> 00:09:35,492
You know there's no way
that Nakahara jumped, right?

72
00:09:35,492 --> 00:09:36,993
I just wish
I would have gotten a picture

73
00:09:36,993 --> 00:09:38,370
of Tozawa
entering the building.

74
00:09:38,370 --> 00:09:41,456
That fucker never
came back out.

75
00:09:41,456 --> 00:09:46,086
I will get back to you
with anything we learn.

76
00:09:46,086 --> 00:09:48,213
And by we,
you mean that female detective

77
00:09:48,213 --> 00:09:50,840
who sent me packing
the other day?

78
00:09:50,840 --> 00:09:52,008
How's that working out?

79
00:09:52,008 --> 00:09:55,095
She's, like, your new partner
or something?

80
00:09:57,138 --> 00:09:59,099
It is working fine.

81
00:09:59,099 --> 00:10:00,350
Great.

82
00:10:00,350 --> 00:10:02,227
But we're still a thing, right?

83
00:10:02,227 --> 00:10:04,312
Starsky and Hutch?

84
00:10:04,312 --> 00:10:07,148
Which of us is Starsky?

85
00:10:07,148 --> 00:10:08,775
Me, obviously.

86
00:10:11,945 --> 00:10:13,863
I do not think so.

87
00:12:16,986 --> 00:12:18,029
Ah.

88
00:12:52,814 --> 00:12:54,315
<i>Hai.</i>

89
00:16:18,895 --> 00:16:21,022
And it's for sure that
this complex is being built

90
00:16:21,022 --> 00:16:22,440
over Shimbashi Station?

91
00:16:22,440 --> 00:16:24,484
Yep, I've seen
the blueprints.

92
00:16:24,484 --> 00:16:25,902
It won't be announced
for a good year,

93
00:16:25,902 --> 00:16:27,529
but that's where it's going.

94
00:16:27,529 --> 00:16:29,114
This anything to do
with Ishida?

95
00:16:29,114 --> 00:16:31,866
Can you just do this for me?

96
00:16:31,866 --> 00:16:33,076
Are you in trouble?

97
00:16:37,539 --> 00:16:39,082
Fine.

98
00:16:39,082 --> 00:16:41,501
I'll follow it up.

99
00:16:49,968 --> 00:16:51,970
What's up with you?

100
00:16:51,970 --> 00:16:55,223
There's something
I need to tell you.

101
00:16:55,223 --> 00:16:57,017
Tozawa's back in Tokyo.

102
00:16:57,017 --> 00:16:58,768
I saw him
at his lawyer's office,

103
00:16:58,768 --> 00:17:02,188
and I followed him to a medical
building in Minato-ku.

104
00:17:02,188 --> 00:17:04,190
I'm gonna make him pay
for what he did.

105
00:17:04,190 --> 00:17:06,776
I'm not giving up.

106
00:17:06,776 --> 00:17:08,820
Jake, I love you
for wanting to take him on,

107
00:17:08,820 --> 00:17:12,407
but having a death wish
isn't sexy.

108
00:17:12,407 --> 00:17:15,952
We had videotape
of his men killing Pol--

109
00:17:15,952 --> 00:17:18,079
no consequences.

110
00:17:18,079 --> 00:17:21,791
His men beat you up--
no consequences.

111
00:17:21,791 --> 00:17:23,668
So no, I'd rather not
find out one day

112
00:17:23,668 --> 00:17:24,878
that you just disappeared,

113
00:17:24,878 --> 00:17:26,629
and there will be
no consequences.

114
00:19:37,844 --> 00:19:39,637
They know the actual location

115
00:19:39,637 --> 00:19:41,389
of where the project is
being built?

116
00:19:41,389 --> 00:19:42,682
Yeah, my source
just called me.

117
00:19:42,682 --> 00:19:44,184
They said Shimbashi.

118
00:19:44,184 --> 00:19:46,644
Are they in
the transport office?

119
00:19:46,644 --> 00:19:49,773
No, they're...
in a different field,

120
00:19:49,773 --> 00:19:51,941
but I trust them.

121
00:19:54,652 --> 00:19:58,281
Maruyama-san?

122
00:19:58,281 --> 00:20:00,658
Have the article ready
for tomorrow's edition.

123
00:20:03,286 --> 00:20:07,624
I was thinking...
Kurihira should do it.

124
00:20:07,624 --> 00:20:10,210
You want to give away
your scoop?

125
00:20:10,210 --> 00:20:12,212
I think
he could really use it.

126
00:20:12,212 --> 00:20:14,464
You know, Baku's been
riding him really hard.

127
00:20:16,216 --> 00:20:18,343
Fine.

128
00:20:18,343 --> 00:20:23,640
Oh, and your request for your
trip to America was approved.

129
00:20:23,640 --> 00:20:24,891
Oh.

130
00:20:24,891 --> 00:20:26,893
Oh, I'm just not sure,
what with everything going on,

131
00:20:26,893 --> 00:20:28,603
that I should go, you know...

132
00:20:28,603 --> 00:20:30,980
Jake, there will
always be stories,

133
00:20:30,980 --> 00:20:33,900
but you have only one family.

134
00:20:39,364 --> 00:20:41,074
The Ministry will say
no comment,

135
00:20:41,074 --> 00:20:42,617
so you'll just need
to bluff a little.

136
00:20:42,617 --> 00:20:43,702
I see.

137
00:20:43,702 --> 00:20:45,161
Make them think
that you already have

138
00:20:45,161 --> 00:20:46,413
proof of the location.

139
00:20:46,413 --> 00:20:48,373
You just need confirmation.

140
00:20:48,373 --> 00:20:49,916
But don't say the name.

141
00:20:49,916 --> 00:20:51,710
- Okay.
- Okay?

142
00:20:51,710 --> 00:20:54,129
Jake-san,
thank you for this tip.

143
00:20:54,129 --> 00:20:56,881
We gotta look out
for each other, right?

144
00:20:56,881 --> 00:20:58,550
You got this.

145
00:21:43,970 --> 00:21:45,180
Ah?

146
00:22:29,099 --> 00:22:30,100
<i>Oi.</i>

147
00:25:31,823 --> 00:25:33,491
- Are you serious?
- Huh?

148
00:25:36,161 --> 00:25:37,454
We are taking them out.

149
00:26:07,233 --> 00:26:09,319
It was temporary.

150
00:26:09,319 --> 00:26:11,196
It doesn't matter.

151
00:26:11,196 --> 00:26:15,825
It isn't really my club,
as you made perfectly clear.

152
00:26:20,413 --> 00:26:22,624
No, no,
it's actually two circles

153
00:26:22,624 --> 00:26:24,751
going in opposite directions.

154
00:26:24,751 --> 00:26:27,629
So let me get this straight.

155
00:26:27,629 --> 00:26:30,215
You're talking about
the Yamanote Line

156
00:26:30,215 --> 00:26:33,718
that makes the big circle
around Tokyo.

157
00:26:33,718 --> 00:26:35,428
Yes.

158
00:26:38,682 --> 00:26:41,476
The outer track runs clockwise,

159
00:26:41,476 --> 00:26:44,813
the inner track
counterclockwise.

160
00:26:44,813 --> 00:26:47,399
So if you prefer foreign men,

161
00:26:47,399 --> 00:26:49,943
we say you ride
the outer track.

162
00:26:49,943 --> 00:26:52,779
So I'm a foreign man.

163
00:26:52,779 --> 00:26:54,531
Well...

164
00:26:57,075 --> 00:27:00,787
And if you stick
to native Japanese men,

165
00:27:00,787 --> 00:27:03,164
you ride the inner track, right?

166
00:27:13,133 --> 00:27:17,053
So I guess
you're a outer track man, huh?

167
00:27:20,348 --> 00:27:23,059
Actually,

168
00:27:23,059 --> 00:27:26,980
tonight was my first time
on that track.

169
00:27:26,980 --> 00:27:28,481
Really?

170
00:27:32,444 --> 00:27:35,071
Thank you.

171
00:27:38,783 --> 00:27:41,661
What about you?

172
00:27:41,661 --> 00:27:43,788
To be honest,

173
00:27:43,788 --> 00:27:47,876
it's been a year
since I've been with anyone.

174
00:27:49,336 --> 00:27:50,795
Really?

175
00:27:50,795 --> 00:27:52,339
Why?

176
00:27:52,339 --> 00:27:55,550
I got tired of not liking
the people in my bed.

177
00:27:57,886 --> 00:27:59,429
Thank you.

178
00:28:05,185 --> 00:28:09,230
It was a big deal for me
to approach you at that party.

179
00:28:12,400 --> 00:28:15,945
I haven't done that
in a long time.

180
00:28:22,619 --> 00:28:26,956
You have a lot of lost time
to make up for.

181
00:28:28,041 --> 00:28:29,584
If you can keep up.

182
00:30:12,979 --> 00:30:16,608
So here's
Tozawa's file, right?

183
00:30:16,608 --> 00:30:19,944
And here are the files
of four other Yaks.

184
00:30:19,944 --> 00:30:22,197
Are you sure they're Yakuza?

185
00:30:22,197 --> 00:30:24,240
Dude, you know
how many fanzines I read.

186
00:30:24,240 --> 00:30:25,784
I know all their names.

187
00:30:33,625 --> 00:30:35,418
Illness of the trade.

188
00:30:35,418 --> 00:30:37,921
We call it shokugoyo.

189
00:30:37,921 --> 00:30:39,839
Yakuza live a life
filled with alcohol,

190
00:30:39,839 --> 00:30:41,841
shabu, and tattoo needles.

191
00:30:41,841 --> 00:30:44,552
Do that long enough
and you get liver disease.

192
00:30:44,552 --> 00:30:47,138
Well, it seems
Tozawa has it--

193
00:30:47,138 --> 00:30:48,223
or did.

194
00:30:48,223 --> 00:30:50,350
It's not something
they get over.

195
00:32:15,977 --> 00:32:16,936
Hayama.

196
00:32:36,498 --> 00:32:37,916
Sato.

197
00:32:41,127 --> 00:32:42,545
<i>Hai.</i>

198
00:33:24,129 --> 00:33:25,213
<i>Iya.</i>

199
00:37:18,071 --> 00:37:19,280
<i>Hai.</i>

200
00:37:38,675 --> 00:37:40,802
Hey!

201
00:37:40,802 --> 00:37:42,095
You want to hit one?

202
00:37:42,095 --> 00:37:44,973
No.

203
00:37:44,973 --> 00:37:46,808
I have a busy night, Meicho.

204
00:37:46,808 --> 00:37:47,934
What's so important?

205
00:37:47,934 --> 00:37:49,519
I got you something.

206
00:37:57,652 --> 00:38:01,823
To thank you for taking care
of that kid in jail.

207
00:38:01,823 --> 00:38:03,116
Oh.

208
00:38:07,328 --> 00:38:08,371
Just one?

209
00:38:08,371 --> 00:38:10,206
One more favor,
and then I give you the other.

210
00:38:16,463 --> 00:38:17,672
Huh.

211
00:38:21,301 --> 00:38:22,969
Oyabuns just give up and die?

212
00:38:22,969 --> 00:38:24,429
I don't believe it.

213
00:38:24,429 --> 00:38:27,766
Some try to fight it
and go to Thailand.

214
00:38:27,766 --> 00:38:29,809
There is a German doctor there.

215
00:38:38,902 --> 00:38:41,780
For... about six months?

216
00:38:41,780 --> 00:38:42,947
Then they die.

217
00:38:50,330 --> 00:38:51,748
Ta-da!

218
00:38:55,418 --> 00:38:57,045
Yeah, not bad.

219
00:38:59,589 --> 00:39:00,840
These are too small.

220
00:39:03,510 --> 00:39:05,261
Hey, wait you got
a little brother, right?

221
00:39:05,261 --> 00:39:06,805
Give 'em to him.

222
00:39:09,099 --> 00:39:10,308
Okay.

223
00:39:15,397 --> 00:39:16,690
- Hey, you want to hit one?
- No, no, no.

224
00:39:16,690 --> 00:39:17,774
Come on, five minutes.

225
00:39:17,774 --> 00:39:19,275
You should practice more.

226
00:39:19,275 --> 00:39:20,610
Thank you.

227
00:40:21,171 --> 00:40:22,589
<i>Aa.</i>

228
00:41:14,599 --> 00:41:15,642
Right?

229
00:41:15,642 --> 00:41:17,644
It's like this rose--

230
00:41:17,644 --> 00:41:18,812
I think it's rose.

231
00:41:18,812 --> 00:41:20,230
I don't know. I have no idea.
You can use it.

232
00:41:20,230 --> 00:41:23,233
Ladies, listen up.

233
00:41:23,233 --> 00:41:24,901
We have a big night tonight.

234
00:41:24,901 --> 00:41:27,696
Important guest.

235
00:41:27,696 --> 00:41:29,072
Is it Liam Gallagher?

236
00:41:30,824 --> 00:41:32,283
It's not Liam Gallagher,

237
00:41:32,283 --> 00:41:34,869
but I do need you all
in top form.

238
00:41:41,459 --> 00:41:42,711
Okay.

239
00:41:46,631 --> 00:41:49,300
Samantha?

240
00:41:49,300 --> 00:41:52,595
What happened
with your architect?

241
00:41:52,595 --> 00:41:56,141
Oh, it's so complicated.

242
00:41:56,141 --> 00:41:59,019
I think tonight,
everything gets sorted.

243
00:41:59,019 --> 00:42:01,771
No more Chihara-kai.

244
00:42:01,771 --> 00:42:03,648
I'm offering Ishida a deal.

245
00:42:03,648 --> 00:42:07,610
And if he takes it,
the club is mine 100%.

246
00:42:07,610 --> 00:42:11,781
Samantha, be smart.

247
00:42:11,781 --> 00:42:14,075
Yakuza do not give things back.

248
00:42:14,075 --> 00:42:15,577
It won't work!

249
00:42:15,577 --> 00:42:17,537
It has to work.

250
00:42:22,459 --> 00:42:24,586
Okay.

251
00:42:24,586 --> 00:42:26,880
Let me run the floor tonight.

252
00:42:26,880 --> 00:42:30,717
Whatever you need,
I'm there for you.

253
00:42:30,717 --> 00:42:32,385
Thank you.

254
00:42:34,929 --> 00:42:36,556
<i>- Hai.
- Arigato.</i>

255
00:42:44,814 --> 00:42:47,567
Is that how we look out
for each other, Jake-san,

256
00:42:47,567 --> 00:42:49,861
by stabbing me in the back?

257
00:42:49,861 --> 00:42:51,029
What are you talking about?

258
00:42:51,029 --> 00:42:54,407
You gave me shit advice
so I would fail.

259
00:42:54,407 --> 00:42:56,868
Dude, I told you
not to say the actual name.

260
00:42:56,868 --> 00:42:58,995
After you did that,
the Ministry had to announce.

261
00:42:58,995 --> 00:43:00,038
That's on you, Tin-Tin.

262
00:44:03,268 --> 00:44:06,271
No matter how this goes,

263
00:44:06,271 --> 00:44:09,357
I'd like to take you
to dinner tomorrow.

264
00:44:09,357 --> 00:44:12,944
A real date.

265
00:44:12,944 --> 00:44:16,281
I don't think the mama-san
is supposed to date clients.

266
00:44:16,281 --> 00:44:20,660
Just one client
who I'm very grateful to

267
00:44:20,660 --> 00:44:22,996
and very attracted to.

268
